## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Build green: backend + frontend
- [x] Repeat-mode rule with `max_fires_per_resolution=3` and
      cooldown bypassed stops at 3 fires (`TestEvaluate_MaxFiresCap_SuppressesAfterCap`)
- [x] Falling edge resets the counter; the next rising edge gets a
      fresh `cap` (`TestEvaluate_MaxFiresCap_FallingEdgeResetsCounter`)
- [x] NULL cap = legacy unlimited (10/10 fires)
      (`TestEvaluate_MaxFiresCap_NullMeansUnlimited`)
- [x] Once-mode rule with non-null cap: latch still wins
      (`TestEvaluate_MaxFiresCap_OnceMode_NoEffect`)
- [x] New `teslasync_cep_rules_max_fires_cap_hit_total` Prometheus
      counter registered (declared in `metrics.go`; verifiable via
      `curl /metrics | grep cep_rules_max_fires_cap_hit_total` once
      the API is up)
- [x] UI hides the input when `trigger_mode === 'once'` (gated via
      `editor.trigger_mode === 'repeat' && (…)` JSX wrapper)

